    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="faradays_law_mass gives the mass of a species deposited or consumed by a constant current over time. This example verifies the linear proportionality to both current and time (Faraday&#x27;s first law), computes the minimum applied voltage needed to force a non-spontaneous (electrolytic) reaction to run, and contrasts a spontaneous galvanic reaction against one that needs external electrolysis.">

